## Smart Planning System

The [ResearchPlanner](file:///c:/Users/emirsyah/Documents/CODING/openta/open-ta-telyu-dspy/backend/app/services/planner.py) produces [SmartPlanStep](file:///c:/Users/emirsyah/Documents/CODING/openta/open-ta-telyu-dspy/backend/app/services/planner.py#20-38) objects with:

| Field | Type | Description |
|-------|------|-------------|
| `step_type` | `research \| synthesis \| comparison \| analysis` | Determines if search is needed |
| `query_strategy` | `single \| multi_query` | Single retrieval vs parallel decomposition |
| `decomposition_hint` | `str \| None` | Hint for QueryDecomposer (e.g., `"methods:SVM,CNN,BERT"`) |
| `focus_area` | `str \| None` | Specific aspect to focus on |

**Heuristic skip**: Simple questions (< 20 words, no comparison keywords) use [default_plan()](file:///c:/Users/emirsyah/Documents/CODING/openta/open-ta-telyu-dspy/backend/app/services/planner.py#150-178) to skip the planner LLM call entirely.

---

## Retrieval Layer

### Single-Query Path
1. **Query generation** → [QueryGenerator](file:///c:/Users/emirsyah/Documents/CODING/openta/open-ta-telyu-dspy/backend/app/services/rag.py#189-216) → optimized keywords
2. **Vector search** → Voyage AI embeds query → PGVector cosine similarity → top-k papers
3. **Zero-result retry** → [QueryReformulator](file:///c:/Users/emirsyah/Documents/CODING/openta/open-ta-telyu-dspy/backend/app/services/rag.py#218-228) → broader query → retry search

### Multi-Query Path (for `query_strategy='multi_query'`)
1. **Decomposition** → [QueryDecomposer](file:///c:/Users/emirsyah/Documents/CODING/openta/open-ta-telyu-dspy/backend/app/services/query_decomposer.py#42-79) → 2-4 sub-queries
2. **Parallel retrieval** → [parallel_retrieve()](file:///c:/Users/emirsyah/Documents/CODING/openta/open-ta-telyu-dspy/backend/app/utils/parallel_retrieve.py) runs all sub-queries concurrently
3. **Deduplication** → merge results across sub-queries

---

## Post-Processing Pipeline

1. **Citation building** — [_build_cited_papers()](file:///c:/Users/emirsyah/Documents/CODING/openta/open-ta-telyu-dspy/backend/app/utils/streaming.py#33-56) maps DSPy-returned source IDs back to retrieved [PaperResult](file:///c:/Users/emirsyah/Documents/CODING/openta/open-ta-telyu-dspy/backend/app/core/models.py#36-39) objects → [CitedPaper](file:///c:/Users/emirsyah/Documents/CODING/openta/open-ta-telyu-dspy/backend/app/core/models.py#159-167) with `citation_number`
2. **Citation audit** — [_audit_citations()](file:///c:/Users/emirsyah/Documents/CODING/openta/open-ta-telyu-dspy/backend/app/utils/streaming.py#67-84) uses regex `\[(\d+)\]` to find all `[N]` references in the answer and flags any N > number of retrieved papers (hallucination detection, zero latency)
3. **Gap detection** — [GapDetector](file:///c:/Users/emirsyah/Documents/CODING/openta/open-ta-telyu-dspy/backend/app/services/rag.py#230-239) checks if the answer fully covers the question; if partial, triggers re-retrieval + re-generation
4. **History persistence** — [_save_history()](file:///c:/Users/emirsyah/Documents/CODING/openta/open-ta-telyu-dspy/backend/app/api/routes/chat.py#36-62) → Redis + DB via `SessionManager`
5. **Title generation** — [TitleGenerationSignature](file:///c:/Users/emirsyah/Documents/CODING/openta/open-ta-telyu-dspy/backend/app/services/rag.py#105-115) on first message only (cheap LM)

---

## Summary: LLM Call Count

> [!IMPORTANT]
> In the worst case (streaming, research question, complex plan, gap detected), the system makes **up to 9+ LLM calls** per user message.

| Call # | What | Model |
|--------|------|-------|
| 1 | Intent classification | cheap |
| 2 | Query generation (parallel with #1) | cheap |
| 3 | Acknowledgment generation | cheap |
| 4 | Plan generation | **main** |
| 5-6 | Step thinking (per step, ~2 steps) | cheap |
| 7 | Query decomposition (if multi_query) | cheap |
| 8 | Final answer (ChainOfThought) | **main** |
| 9 | Gap detection | cheap |
| 10 | Refinement answer (if gap found) | **main** |
| 11 | Title generation (first message) | cheap |
